1
00:00:18,810 --> 00:00:23,850
Match 9 ends in a draw, with Team Y's Niko scoring against Team W.

2
00:00:23,940 --> 00:00:28,270
As a result, we're in 3rd place,

3
00:00:28,360 --> 00:00:32,780
and our match is the final one in Building 5.

4
00:00:32,860 --> 00:00:36,200
If we draw, we'll fall behind on goal difference.

5
00:00:36,870 --> 00:00:39,790
In short, to survive, we must win.

6
00:00:39,870 --> 00:00:41,000
It's that simple.

7
00:00:41,620 --> 00:00:43,620
Hey, Kuon is listening to us.

8
00:00:43,710 --> 00:00:44,540
Should I kill him?

9
00:00:44,620 --> 00:00:47,380
Forget it. No one's going to make a deal with him anyway.

10
00:00:47,460 --> 00:00:50,800
But Team Y managed to get a good draw.

11
00:00:50,880 --> 00:00:55,760
More importantly, was Niko ever the type to score a goal like that himself?

12
00:00:55,840 --> 00:00:58,680
Seems like he was inspired by someone.

13
00:00:59,180 --> 00:01:01,720
There are those who get stronger after losing.

14
00:01:02,270 --> 00:01:05,480
Now, regarding the key player for Team V,

15
00:01:05,560 --> 00:01:07,060
our opponent in the final match.

16
00:01:07,150 --> 00:01:10,480
This ridiculously good attacking trio

17
00:01:10,570 --> 00:01:14,280
that scored 18 goals in 3 matches.

18
00:01:14,860 --> 00:01:17,110
Tsurugi Zantetsu, 5 goals.

19
00:01:17,700 --> 00:01:19,830
Mikage Reo, 6 goals.

20
00:01:19,910 --> 00:01:24,120
Finally, the team's best, Nagi Seishiro, 7 goals.

21
00:01:24,710 --> 00:01:27,460
If we can't stop these three, we'll never win.

22
00:01:29,790 --> 00:01:31,840
If you can't win without it being a hassle,

23
00:01:31,920 --> 00:01:33,670
you must be weak. What a pain.

24
00:01:34,550 --> 00:01:36,300
Nagi Seishiro.

25
00:01:36,380 --> 00:01:37,970
He's pissing me off.

26
00:01:38,890 --> 00:01:40,850
I will definitely win!

27
00:03:20,360 --> 00:03:21,820
Hey, Nagi.

28
00:03:21,910 --> 00:03:24,370
You skipped practice early again today.

29
00:03:25,080 --> 00:03:28,080
Yeah, it seemed like a hassle.

30
00:03:28,160 --> 00:03:29,540
You know what?

31
00:03:29,620 --> 00:03:31,170
If you skip practice like that,

32
00:03:31,250 --> 00:03:34,750
the lactic acid in your knees will turn into a bad glucosamine flare-up.

33
00:03:35,420 --> 00:03:36,880
So, did I say it right?

34
00:03:36,960 --> 00:03:38,420
Yeah, sure.

35
00:03:39,720 --> 00:03:43,800
You idiot, Zantetsu. Nagi doesn't even need to practice.

36
00:03:43,890 --> 00:03:47,100
You're spoiling Nagi too much, Reo.

37
00:03:47,180 --> 00:03:48,350
Of course.

38
00:03:48,930 --> 00:03:50,310
He is my...

39
00:03:51,230 --> 00:03:52,810
Treasure, after all.

40
00:03:56,230 --> 00:03:59,900
My life was nothing but boring.

41
00:04:00,780 --> 00:04:01,950
Reo.

42
00:04:02,030 --> 00:04:04,910
You were born to surpass me.

43
00:04:04,990 --> 00:04:07,870
Everything in this world exists solely for you.

44
00:04:07,950 --> 00:04:09,830
Enough already, dear.

45
00:04:09,910 --> 00:04:12,160
Reo, is there anything you want?

46
00:04:13,870 --> 00:04:14,830
I'm bored.

47
00:04:14,920 --> 00:04:15,920
So boring.

48
00:04:16,880 --> 00:04:19,760
I had everything I wanted.

49
00:04:19,840 --> 00:04:23,680
You're the top of the class again. You're so amazing, Reo-chan.

50
00:04:24,550 --> 00:04:28,180
But I couldn't find what I truly wanted there.

51
00:04:28,260 --> 00:04:29,520
What are you saying?

52
00:04:29,600 --> 00:04:31,930
Things that come too easily are just boring.

53
00:04:34,650 --> 00:04:38,770
I wanted a treasure that belongs only to me.

54
00:04:47,620 --> 00:04:48,660
That's it.

55
00:04:49,450 --> 00:04:50,660
I want this!

56
00:04:52,710 --> 00:04:54,250
No, absolutely not.

57
00:04:55,040 --> 00:04:56,170
But why?

58
00:04:56,250 --> 00:04:58,420
You said I could have anything I wanted.

59
00:04:59,040 --> 00:05:01,010
You are my heir.

60
00:05:01,090 --> 00:05:02,760
And to be a soccer player,

61
00:05:02,840 --> 00:05:04,680
you need innate talent.

62
00:05:04,760 --> 00:05:07,260
Even if you started now, you wouldn't achieve anything.

63
00:05:07,340 --> 00:05:10,560
Your father is right, Reo. Become a first-class businessman.

64
00:05:10,640 --> 00:05:12,890
I'm telling you this for your own good.

65
00:05:14,770 --> 00:05:16,980
What those people give me...

66
00:05:18,480 --> 00:05:20,730
It's not what I want.

67
00:05:22,480 --> 00:05:25,530
I'm going to lead this school to a national championship.

68
00:05:25,610 --> 00:05:27,870
That will shut them up.

69
00:05:28,410 --> 00:05:29,870
The World Cup is next.

70
00:05:31,080 --> 00:05:35,410
But since this is a prep school, their soccer program is weak.

71
00:05:37,290 --> 00:05:40,290
What should I do? I absolutely don't want to give up.

72
00:05:41,000 --> 00:05:42,800
My head hurts.

73
00:05:43,710 --> 00:05:44,920
Sorry.

74
00:05:53,350 --> 00:05:55,980
Amazing! What a great catch.

75
00:05:56,060 --> 00:05:57,520
Oh, I'm not dead.

76
00:05:57,600 --> 00:06:00,650
That was amazing just now! Are you on the soccer team?

77
00:06:00,730 --> 00:06:02,070
I'm dead.

78
00:06:02,150 --> 00:06:04,440
Besides, who are you? Will you play soccer with me?

79
00:06:04,530 --> 00:06:07,530
Ah, the rich man's son.

80
00:06:07,610 --> 00:06:09,410
-Just give me money.
-What?

81
00:06:09,490 --> 00:06:13,410
I don't want to play soccer or anything. I've never even played sports before.

82
00:06:14,370 --> 00:06:17,210
I just want to live my life without a care in the world.

83
00:06:17,830 --> 00:06:18,960
So give me some money.

84
00:06:21,000 --> 00:06:24,300
No way. That control and your physique just now...

85
00:06:24,380 --> 00:06:26,260
I'm sure you have talent!

86
00:06:26,340 --> 00:06:29,470
Let's play soccer together! You could even go pro!

87
00:06:30,090 --> 00:06:32,180
Can't I just not do it?

88
00:06:32,260 --> 00:06:34,180
Soccer sounds like a hassle.

89
00:06:35,430 --> 00:06:37,270
I don't like troublesome things.

90
00:06:37,350 --> 00:06:39,230
I don't want to work at it.

91
00:06:39,310 --> 00:06:41,650
If you have no talent, you can't do it.

92
00:06:42,400 --> 00:06:46,190
Right there, a talented person is standing right in front of me.

93
00:06:48,150 --> 00:06:49,660
I want him!

94
00:06:51,410 --> 00:06:52,870
I like you!

95
00:06:52,950 --> 00:06:54,450
You don't have to change.

96
00:06:55,620 --> 00:06:58,000
My life was nothing but boring.

97
00:06:58,620 --> 00:07:01,000
Let's play soccer together!

98
00:07:01,790 --> 00:07:04,750
Until I met soccer and Nagi Seishiro.

99
00:07:11,010 --> 00:07:13,350
That's your 'I wonder if we can win the next match?' look!

100
00:07:13,430 --> 00:07:15,100
'I have a stomach ache!' look!

101
00:07:15,180 --> 00:07:17,720
'I wonder if grandma is okay?' look.

102
00:07:17,810 --> 00:07:18,770
All wrong!

103
00:07:18,850 --> 00:07:22,190
The correct answer was 'What does rain taste like?'

104
00:07:22,270 --> 00:07:23,523
How the hell would we know that!

105
00:07:23,560 --> 00:07:26,730
The Wanima Brothers' 'What's That Look Like?' game!

106
00:07:26,820 --> 00:07:28,280
What the hell are you guys doing?

107
00:07:28,360 --> 00:07:29,950
Focus a little!

108
00:07:30,950 --> 00:07:32,910
'I'm very angry!' look.

109
00:07:32,990 --> 00:07:34,870
That's not for your look game!

110
00:07:34,950 --> 00:07:37,740
Let's just have a strategy meeting for now.

111
00:07:38,790 --> 00:07:39,960
Hold on a sec.

112
00:07:41,080 --> 00:07:43,460
I still haven't forgiven this bastard.

113
00:07:45,960 --> 00:07:49,090
After all, he'll just leak our tactics again!

114
00:07:50,470 --> 00:07:53,340
Come on, let's all hit him one by one!

115
00:07:53,430 --> 00:07:54,600
Great idea, Raichi!

116
00:07:54,680 --> 00:07:56,050
It's judgment time!

117
00:07:56,140 --> 00:07:57,510
Hey, cut it out!

118
00:07:57,600 --> 00:07:59,850
-What if he gets injured?
-Huh?

119
00:07:59,930 --> 00:08:03,560
I'm saying we can't beat Team V if we don't have 11 players!

120
00:08:04,940 --> 00:08:05,940
Are you stupid?

121
00:08:06,020 --> 00:08:07,440
I'm not playing!

122
00:08:09,780 --> 00:08:15,200
Even if Team Z loses at this rate, I'll win as top scorer with 3 goals.

123
00:08:15,280 --> 00:08:18,160
Doing nothing is the best option for me.

124
00:08:18,240 --> 00:08:20,250
Yeah, I'm definitely going to kill you!

125
00:08:20,330 --> 00:08:21,620
I said stop it!

126
00:08:21,710 --> 00:08:25,130
Then, in the next match, if I score 3 goals,

127
00:08:25,210 --> 00:08:28,000
I'll take the privilege with 4 goals total.

128
00:08:28,090 --> 00:08:30,880
Do you still not want to play?

129
00:08:31,970 --> 00:08:35,340
Playing 11 vs. 10 against Team V...

130
00:08:35,430 --> 00:08:36,680
I'll score.

131
00:08:36,760 --> 00:08:39,560
I'll destroy you fair and square.

132
00:08:40,470 --> 00:08:43,060
Try it if you can.

133
00:08:44,980 --> 00:08:49,400
You can't play soccer alone. I know that better than anyone.

134
00:08:50,860 --> 00:08:52,280
What do you mean?

135
00:08:52,360 --> 00:08:53,530
Shut up.

136
00:08:54,320 --> 00:08:57,280
I always took soccer seriously,

137
00:08:58,370 --> 00:09:01,750
working hard with the goal of winning the World Cup.

138
00:09:01,830 --> 00:09:03,830
We can't catch up to you, Kuon.

139
00:09:03,910 --> 00:09:05,750
You're too serious.

140
00:09:05,830 --> 00:09:08,790
National championship, Japan National Team, and all that...

141
00:09:08,880 --> 00:09:12,590
You were the only one taking those things seriously, Kuon-senpai.

142
00:09:15,800 --> 00:09:17,430
It can't end in a place like this.

143
00:09:18,390 --> 00:09:21,270
I'm sick of losing because of my team.

144
00:09:21,350 --> 00:09:22,720
Shut up, you bastard!

145
00:09:23,310 --> 00:09:26,060
Traitors can't become the best in the world or anything like that!

146
00:09:26,140 --> 00:09:27,770
Say whatever you want.

147
00:09:27,850 --> 00:09:30,190
I won't be seeing you again anyway.

148
00:09:30,270 --> 00:09:31,190
You bastard!

149
00:09:31,280 --> 00:09:32,780
Wait a sec.

150
00:09:32,860 --> 00:09:37,820
If there are two players with the most goals, who wins?

151
00:09:37,910 --> 00:09:40,910
I think it was the one with fewer yellow cards.

152
00:09:40,990 --> 00:09:42,830
What if that's also tied?

153
00:09:43,450 --> 00:09:46,710
The player with the higher Blue Lock rank wins.

154
00:09:46,790 --> 00:09:49,880
Hey there, what's up? It's me, Ego Jinpachi.

155
00:09:49,960 --> 00:09:54,170
If you lose, and both your goals and penalty points are tied,

156
00:09:54,260 --> 00:09:58,430
the one with the highest rank will win.

157
00:10:00,300 --> 00:10:02,180
See, I'm in first place.

158
00:10:02,260 --> 00:10:06,390
Why? Why is this traitorous bastard at the top!

159
00:10:06,480 --> 00:10:11,020
Since goals were the only thing that mattered in the first selections,

160
00:10:11,110 --> 00:10:13,320
there's no problem according to the rules.

161
00:10:13,820 --> 00:10:15,690
But Kuon Wataru,

162
00:10:16,530 --> 00:10:19,450
as a forward, you're the lowest of the low.

163
00:10:19,530 --> 00:10:21,740
Or rather, all of you are pathetic.

164
00:10:24,080 --> 00:10:27,330
In this life-or-death game, you think you've survived,

165
00:10:27,410 --> 00:10:29,830
but you've only made it this far by chance.

166
00:10:29,920 --> 00:10:32,670
A game like that has no value.

167
00:10:33,590 --> 00:10:38,840
What the world's best striker needs is the ability to reproduce the same goal.

168
00:10:40,090 --> 00:10:43,560
Even if a spectacular goal has a huge impact,

169
00:10:43,640 --> 00:10:47,560
there are people all over the world who can score such a goal just once.

170
00:10:47,640 --> 00:10:51,310
Why can't you reproduce the same goal?

171
00:10:51,400 --> 00:10:54,900
Because those goals were all just luck.

172
00:10:55,480 --> 00:10:57,530
Especially someone who scores by betraying others...

173
00:10:57,610 --> 00:10:59,360
that's trash that will never be able to reproduce that goal.

174
00:11:00,450 --> 00:11:05,740
What you need right now is the formula for how you can score.

175
00:11:06,790 --> 00:11:09,870
Research when and in what situation

176
00:11:09,960 --> 00:11:11,770
your weapon allows you to score a goal.

177
00:11:13,000 --> 00:11:14,710
How far were you from the goal?

178
00:11:15,300 --> 00:11:16,840
How many defenders were there?

179
00:11:16,920 --> 00:11:18,220
Where did you receive the pass?

180
00:11:18,300 --> 00:11:20,300
What were you feeling at that moment?

181
00:11:20,380 --> 00:11:23,390
Engrave every detail into your mind.

182
00:11:24,100 --> 00:11:29,060
Positioning, control, dribbling, shooting...

183
00:11:29,140 --> 00:11:32,730
Find the formula that makes you stand out the most.

184
00:11:32,810 --> 00:11:36,900
Every world-famous striker has their own formula.

185
00:11:38,570 --> 00:11:41,450
You are still just relying on luck.

186
00:11:41,530 --> 00:11:43,450
You can't go on like this.

187
00:11:43,530 --> 00:11:48,540
Unless you can reproduce it, you can't evolve. Get that into your heads!

188
00:11:49,910 --> 00:11:52,750
Uncontrollable events happen during a match.

189
00:11:53,420 --> 00:11:57,960
Those who have proven their formula on such a battlefield,

190
00:11:58,050 --> 00:12:01,340
who can turn it into a goal,

191
00:12:01,430 --> 00:12:04,300
are only the world's best.

192
00:12:05,430 --> 00:12:07,100
Don't leave your work to luck.

193
00:12:07,180 --> 00:12:09,430
Win as if it were second nature!

194
00:12:14,860 --> 00:12:18,780
Anyway, Kuon, in the next match, don't you move from your spot.

195
00:12:23,610 --> 00:12:25,700
The reproducibility of goals...

196
00:12:25,780 --> 00:12:29,540
In other words, a weapon you can definitely use regardless of the situation or how many times.

197
00:12:29,620 --> 00:12:31,540
We can't leave this to luck.

198
00:12:32,120 --> 00:12:33,710
My weapon is spatial awareness,

199
00:12:34,420 --> 00:12:37,290
but on my own, I'm powerless.

200
00:12:37,380 --> 00:12:39,800
I don't think we can beat them like this.

201
00:12:40,510 --> 00:12:44,430
If we don't evolve, we can't win.

202
00:12:45,550 --> 00:12:47,350
If we don't evolve, we can't win.

203
00:12:56,690 --> 00:12:59,400
BUILDING 5 FIRST SELECTION - TOP SCORER - 10 GOALS

204
00:12:59,480 --> 00:13:01,360
What is it, loser?

205
00:13:02,110 --> 00:13:03,780
What the hell do you want?

206
00:13:03,860 --> 00:13:06,910
TEAM X - BAROU SHOUEI

207
00:13:14,000 --> 00:13:15,580
Teach me, Barou.

208
00:13:15,670 --> 00:13:17,920
What can I do to become like you?

209
00:13:22,670 --> 00:13:24,260
Give me a break.

210
00:13:24,340 --> 00:13:26,720
Go find it yourself, loser.

211
00:13:26,800 --> 00:13:28,220
Wait!

212
00:13:28,300 --> 00:13:30,560
You can score goals on your own, too.

213
00:13:30,640 --> 00:13:33,310
Among the people I know, you're the best.

214
00:13:33,390 --> 00:13:36,600
I don't want this to end! I want to win.

215
00:13:36,690 --> 00:13:39,400
I want to become someone who can fight on his own.

216
00:13:41,530 --> 00:13:43,440
Hey, you brainless fool.

217
00:13:43,530 --> 00:13:46,660
I'll destroy that garbage dreamer ego of yours

218
00:13:46,740 --> 00:13:49,370
right here!

219
00:13:49,450 --> 00:13:50,950
One-on-one?

220
00:13:51,030 --> 00:13:52,660
I can't win on physical strength.

221
00:13:52,740 --> 00:13:55,650
I have to focus on his feet and the ball and steal it when I get the chance.

222
00:13:56,040 --> 00:13:57,870
When he makes his move to pass me!

223
00:13:57,960 --> 00:13:58,960
Here!

224
00:14:01,290 --> 00:14:03,090
He hasn't passed yet!

225
00:14:08,720 --> 00:14:12,510
He smashed it into the top corner from over 20 meters away?

226
00:14:12,600 --> 00:14:14,140
His accuracy is insane.

227
00:14:14,220 --> 00:14:15,680
See ya, loser.

228
00:14:15,770 --> 00:14:16,980
Wait!

229
00:14:17,060 --> 00:14:18,690
One more time! Please!

230
00:14:18,770 --> 00:14:20,940
Come at me! It's not over yet!

231
00:14:21,520 --> 00:14:23,940
Who the hell do you think you're talking to?

232
00:14:25,440 --> 00:14:27,110
I am the king!

233
00:14:27,200 --> 00:14:28,910
I won't lose this time.

234
00:14:28,990 --> 00:14:31,280
I'll stick to his ass so he can't score.

235
00:14:32,490 --> 00:14:34,200
Shit, he's going to shoot!

236
00:14:34,290 --> 00:14:36,160
But I can just barely reach it...

237
00:14:37,790 --> 00:14:38,960
A feint?

238
00:14:45,590 --> 00:14:48,590
Wow. Is he deliberately aiming for the same spot?

239
00:14:49,180 --> 00:14:51,140
This is the end, loser.

240
00:14:52,050 --> 00:14:56,680
The moment he finds a tiny opening, he fires it in.

241
00:14:57,270 --> 00:14:59,140
That's Barou Shouei for you.

242
00:14:59,230 --> 00:15:01,440
A goal formula.

243
00:15:01,520 --> 00:15:03,190
Wait.

244
00:15:03,270 --> 00:15:06,480
If even Barou has a formula...

245
00:15:09,700 --> 00:15:11,030
I'll stop it this time.

246
00:15:11,110 --> 00:15:12,740
Bring it on, 'king'.

247
00:15:12,820 --> 00:15:14,410
I've figured you out.

248
00:15:14,990 --> 00:15:16,660
Stop barking, you mediocre piece of trash.

249
00:15:17,370 --> 00:15:18,830
Know your place.

250
00:15:20,790 --> 00:15:25,170
If my predictions are correct, he still can't shoot right now.

251
00:15:25,250 --> 00:15:29,590
Slightly to the left of center. Between 40 and 45 degrees.

252
00:15:30,630 --> 00:15:32,550
23 meters.

253
00:15:32,640 --> 00:15:36,680
From there, he'll fire a curved shot into the top right corner.

254
00:15:36,770 --> 00:15:39,020
Barou's absolute scoring distance!

255
00:15:39,100 --> 00:15:40,230
He still can't shoot.

256
00:15:40,850 --> 00:15:43,980
Just as I predicted, he can't score from everywhere.

257
00:15:44,060 --> 00:15:46,360
What allows Barou to score this many goals

258
00:15:46,440 --> 00:15:50,150
is that he has a zone with a high scoring potential.

259
00:15:50,780 --> 00:15:54,160
But in a normal match with opponents, he can't easily enter that zone.

260
00:15:55,200 --> 00:15:57,790
He covers this weakness with his momentary bursts of speed.

261
00:15:57,870 --> 00:16:01,460
That's why he needs that kind of physique!

262
00:16:03,670 --> 00:16:06,380
He gives his all to enter this zone,

263
00:16:06,960 --> 00:16:08,550
and reproduces his goals.

264
00:16:09,420 --> 00:16:11,130
That's the secret of his formula.

265
00:16:11,800 --> 00:16:13,510
Only I can understand it!

266
00:16:13,590 --> 00:16:17,060
If I don't let him into this zone, I can stop him!

267
00:16:17,760 --> 00:16:19,680
Don't get the wrong idea, loser.

268
00:16:19,770 --> 00:16:21,270
My range...

269
00:16:21,350 --> 00:16:23,060
is 27 meters!

270
00:16:28,820 --> 00:16:30,400
Is he a monster?

271
00:16:31,030 --> 00:16:32,030
He's truly...

272
00:16:32,740 --> 00:16:33,990
amazing!

273
00:16:34,570 --> 00:16:37,660
Thanks for teaching me, Barou.

274
00:16:37,740 --> 00:16:39,370
I didn't teach you anything.

275
00:16:39,450 --> 00:16:43,580
I just reminded you that I am the one on the pitch.

276
00:16:43,670 --> 00:16:45,880
That's a pretty good enough reason

277
00:16:45,960 --> 00:16:47,920
for brainless fools to quit soccer, isn't it?

278
00:16:48,630 --> 00:16:50,010
Look at that.

279
00:16:51,300 --> 00:16:53,380
Thank you anyway!

280
00:17:06,100 --> 00:17:09,610
Only 20 hours left until the final match.

281
00:17:10,190 --> 00:17:11,030
ABSOLUTE WEAPON

282
00:17:11,110 --> 00:17:13,700
I understand Barou's goal formula, but...

283
00:17:14,450 --> 00:17:17,620
It's not a weapon I can copy.

284
00:17:18,280 --> 00:17:21,120
My weapon is spatial awareness.

285
00:17:21,200 --> 00:17:24,910
But it doesn't help me score goals on my own.

286
00:17:25,540 --> 00:17:28,040
I have no choice but to find it during the match.

287
00:17:30,380 --> 00:17:32,170
Am I... scared?

288
00:17:33,630 --> 00:17:35,930
Everything will be decided tomorrow.

289
00:17:36,010 --> 00:17:38,510
My career could be over.

290
00:17:39,260 --> 00:17:41,600
If we lose, then again...

291
00:17:46,560 --> 00:17:48,020
Hey, Isagi.

292
00:17:48,770 --> 00:17:52,280
Everything will be decided tomorrow, right?

293
00:17:52,360 --> 00:17:53,360
Igaguri.

294
00:17:54,940 --> 00:17:57,240
I'm too scared to sleep.

295
00:17:57,320 --> 00:18:00,700
If I fail at soccer, I'll have to take over the family temple.

296
00:18:01,490 --> 00:18:04,200
Blue Lock is my last chance.

297
00:18:04,790 --> 00:18:08,540
So having your dream come to an end is that terrifying...

298
00:18:11,170 --> 00:18:12,460
I get it.

299
00:18:12,550 --> 00:18:14,050
I'm trembling because I'm scared.

300
00:18:15,590 --> 00:18:18,130
No, you're right.

301
00:18:18,220 --> 00:18:19,140
What?

302
00:18:19,840 --> 00:18:22,180
We fight because we're scared.

303
00:18:22,810 --> 00:18:24,640
We get stronger because we're scared.

304
00:18:25,390 --> 00:18:26,520
Isagi.

305
00:18:27,100 --> 00:18:28,310
We will definitely win.

306
00:18:29,560 --> 00:18:32,400
Our end hasn't come yet.

307
00:18:40,740 --> 00:18:42,030
We'll advance with the trio

308
00:18:42,120 --> 00:18:46,580
of Kunigami, Gagamaru, and Chigiri, who have high scoring abilities.

309
00:18:46,660 --> 00:18:49,040
Since the opponent plays very offensively,

310
00:18:49,120 --> 00:18:53,210
we'll focus on defense and prevent them from breaking through.

311
00:18:53,290 --> 00:18:54,130
Then,

312
00:18:54,210 --> 00:18:57,380
we'll try to score on the first counter-attack.

313
00:18:57,470 --> 00:19:00,930
This is the only way for the 10 of us to win.

314
00:19:01,010 --> 00:19:04,810
Hey, Kuon. I don't want to see even your shadow on the pitch for 90 minutes.

315
00:19:04,890 --> 00:19:07,390
Don't get involved in anything, you bastard.

316
00:19:07,480 --> 00:19:09,520
If you touch the ball, I'll kill you.

317
00:19:09,600 --> 00:19:11,190
You don't have to tell me.

318
00:19:11,270 --> 00:19:14,360
I don't want to enter the second selection injured.

319
00:19:14,440 --> 00:19:16,940
Since the opposing team is guaranteed to win,

320
00:19:17,030 --> 00:19:18,320
we can find an opening.

321
00:19:18,400 --> 00:19:20,610
If we can seize that, we can win!

322
00:19:20,700 --> 00:19:21,740
Let's do this!

323
00:19:21,820 --> 00:19:22,950
It's finally time.

324
00:19:23,030 --> 00:19:23,950
Let's go.

325
00:19:24,030 --> 00:19:25,030
Yeah.

326
00:19:31,210 --> 00:19:33,380
We're winning this, Team Z!

327
00:19:33,460 --> 00:19:34,460
-Yeah!
-Yeah!

328
00:19:36,420 --> 00:19:38,340
If we don't win, everything ends.

329
00:19:38,420 --> 00:19:42,220
My entire career rests on this final match!

330
00:19:42,800 --> 00:19:43,970
Look, Isagi.

331
00:19:44,550 --> 00:19:46,390
If we lose, will we never see each other again

332
00:19:46,470 --> 00:19:48,560
and never be able to play soccer together?

333
00:19:49,310 --> 00:19:50,310
Bachira.

334
00:19:50,390 --> 00:19:53,940
That's too sad, so I'm going to give it my all.

335
00:19:55,320 --> 00:19:57,030
Exactly. Let's win.

336
00:20:17,630 --> 00:20:18,760
Bring it on.

337
00:20:19,670 --> 00:20:21,470
We are the ones who will win!

338
00:20:27,140 --> 00:20:29,930
We've thoroughly looked over Team V's tactics.

339
00:20:30,020 --> 00:20:32,440
Their playmaker...

340
00:20:32,520 --> 00:20:33,480
is this guy.

341
00:20:33,560 --> 00:20:35,650
BL RANK 222 - MIKAGE REO

342
00:20:35,730 --> 00:20:38,230
Just as I thought, I'm no match for him.

343
00:20:38,320 --> 00:20:40,940
But we can't leave this guy, who delivers the passes that lead to goals,

344
00:20:41,030 --> 00:20:42,820
free in the midfield.

345
00:20:42,900 --> 00:20:45,160
I'll hold him down together with Bachira.

346
00:20:45,780 --> 00:20:46,870
Nice!

347
00:20:46,950 --> 00:20:50,750
When they can't advance, the one who comes to their rescue

348
00:20:50,830 --> 00:20:52,250
is the left-footed speed freak.

349
00:20:52,330 --> 00:20:53,960
BL RANK 223 - TSURUGI ZANTETSU

350
00:20:54,040 --> 00:20:55,630
This guy's goal formula

351
00:20:55,710 --> 00:20:58,840
is his cut-in shots from the right flank at a sharp angle.

352
00:20:58,920 --> 00:21:02,470
But we've completely shut down that route with two defenders.

353
00:21:02,550 --> 00:21:03,800
In that case...

354
00:21:03,880 --> 00:21:05,300
Just as I predicted!

355
00:21:05,930 --> 00:21:08,260
BL RANK 221 - NAGI SEISHIRO

356
00:21:08,350 --> 00:21:10,600
-Igaguri!
-That's it!

357
00:21:10,680 --> 00:21:12,350
We intercepted it here!

358
00:21:12,430 --> 00:21:13,310
Shit!

359
00:21:13,390 --> 00:21:14,850
Get it, Isagi!

360
00:21:14,940 --> 00:21:15,810
Alright!

361
00:21:15,900 --> 00:21:17,020
Time for a counter.

362
00:21:17,610 --> 00:21:18,610
Bachira!

363
00:21:19,440 --> 00:21:21,230
Alright! I'm off.

364
00:21:22,280 --> 00:21:26,070
To not disrupt our defense, we'll attack with few players.

365
00:21:27,320 --> 00:21:28,620
A strong defense...

366
00:21:28,700 --> 00:21:30,870
and a lethal counter with a long pass!

367
00:21:30,950 --> 00:21:33,250
It's up to you, Gagamaru.

368
00:21:33,330 --> 00:21:34,750
Can I reach it?

369
00:21:34,830 --> 00:21:36,290
I can just barely... as myself...

370
00:21:36,370 --> 00:21:37,500
with my foot...

371
00:21:37,580 --> 00:21:40,800
No, a header is best!

372
00:21:45,090 --> 00:21:46,260
That was close!

373
00:21:46,340 --> 00:21:48,040
-But the tactic is working.
-That was good.

374
00:21:48,070 --> 00:21:48,950
I'll score the next one.

375
00:21:48,970 --> 00:21:50,970
-Let's go!
-One more time!

376
00:21:56,640 --> 00:21:59,110
Amazing! This is so much fun!

377
00:22:00,570 --> 00:22:02,940
Hey, Nagi! Let's try that too!

378
00:22:04,190 --> 00:22:05,650
What a hassle.

379
00:22:07,110 --> 00:22:08,280
What?

380
00:22:08,360 --> 00:22:09,620
What are they talking about?

381
00:22:10,740 --> 00:22:15,460
Are they copying our deadly counter-attack?

382
00:22:15,540 --> 00:22:17,460
He hit it too hard! It's going to go out!

383
00:22:29,640 --> 00:22:30,720
How did he reach that ball?

384
00:22:31,600 --> 00:22:33,930
What the hell is this monster?

385
00:22:46,650 --> 00:22:47,990
That was easy.

386
00:22:48,570 --> 00:22:50,570
How did you miss that?

387
00:22:55,870 --> 00:22:58,040
What a monster...

388
00:23:01,790 --> 00:23:04,250
Blue Lock, Extra Time.

389
00:23:04,960 --> 00:23:08,420
Hey, Reo. What were the rules of soccer again?

390
00:23:08,510 --> 00:23:12,350
You just score goals from my passes and forget the rest.

391
00:23:12,970 --> 00:23:15,520
Hey, Nagi. Whose teeth are better?

392
00:23:17,180 --> 00:23:19,350
That's a hassle, you decide for me.

393
00:23:20,190 --> 00:23:22,150
I'm tired from practice.

394
00:23:23,480 --> 00:23:27,110
Let's take a little break. Come on, I'll give you a piggyback ride.

395
00:23:27,190 --> 00:23:29,490
My muscles hurt.

396
00:23:29,570 --> 00:23:30,660
Here?

397
00:23:30,740 --> 00:23:32,660
A little lower.

398
00:23:32,740 --> 00:23:34,160
That must be because you're improving.

399
00:23:34,740 --> 00:23:36,540
Are you coming to practice again tomorrow?

400
00:23:38,700 --> 00:23:41,540
Seriously, soccer is such a pain.

401
00:23:41,620 --> 00:23:43,960
I'll come pick you up after class, okay?

402
00:23:45,460 --> 00:23:47,210
What a hassle.